course: dictionary
lesson: 14724
title: Words for skill and proficiency
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Proficiency is a noun, and it means a high level of skill or ability in something. When you are very good at reading, you have reading proficiency. «She showed great proficiency in swimming.» This means she was very good at swimming.
explain: The word can also mean a test or badge that shows you have reached a certain level. «He earned his swimming proficiency badge» means he passed a test to show he could swim well. The clues are the words around it: a badge, a test, or a level tell you this second meaning.
explain: Look at the word after «in». In «proficiency in maths», the subject tells you what the skill is about. To check your meaning, swap in the word skill: «great skill in swimming» still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: Proficiency means a high level of skill or ability in something.
fact: Proficiency can also mean a test or badge showing that you have reached a certain level, as in «a swimming proficiency badge».
fact: Scouts and Guides earn proficiency badges, and some cyclists take a «cycling proficiency» test in the UK.
fact: Useful phrases are «proficiency in», «a proficiency test» and «level of proficiency».
fact: Synonyms for the skill meaning include skill, ability and expertise, but proficiency often means you have reached a set level.
exercise: «She showed great proficiency in swimming.» What does proficiency mean here? | A feeling of being very tired | A long wait | * A high level of skill | A loud noise
exercise: Sam earned a «cycling proficiency» certificate. What does this suggest? | A race he lost badly | * A test showing he had reached a certain level of skill | A road sign for cars | A new bicycle bell
exercise: Which word could replace proficiency in «Her reading proficiency is growing fast»? | * Skill | Noise | Sleepiness | Mess
test:
What does «proficiency» mean in «a swimming proficiency badge»? | * A badge that shows you have reached a certain level | A badge given for being late | A badge shaped like a fish | A badge for losing a race
Which phrase shows high proficiency in English? | * You speak and write English very well | You are in a hurry to finish English | Your English book is very loud | You were late for English
exam: Which sentence uses proficiency correctly? | I proficiency my dinner quickly. | The proficiency ran down the hill. | * Her proficiency in French impressed the teacher. | The sky was proficiency and blue.
